{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/zihwje10","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":72,"top":422,"width":650,"height":40},"text":"Why not NoiseLearnerV3 here?","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":26,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#161616","bold":true,"alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"textbox","id":"sh/n2lo3qp4","slideIndex":3,"position":{"left":72,"top":470,"width":1080,"height":90},"text":"Its official workflow submits learning jobs to IBM Quantum. No IBM account is configured on this computer, so local rates are simulated inputs, not hardware measurements.","geometry":"rect","lineWidth":0,"style":{"fontSize":22,"typeface":"Arial","color":"#525252","alignment":"left"}}
{"kind":"notes","id":"nt/j13n9z","slideIndex":3,"text":"SLC assigns importance to candidate Pauli error terms and can trade a bounded bias for lower sampling cost. PNA propagates the inverse of learned noise into an observable. The official NoiseLearnerV3 accepts an IBM Quantum backend/service job; IBM documents that it has no local fake-backend mode. Sources: https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-slc/guides/quickstart.html ; https://qiskit.github.io/qiskit-addon-pna/tutorials/01_generate_noise_mitigating_observable.html ; https://quantum.cloud.ibm.com/docs/en/guides/migrate-to-client-side-primitives"}
